\section{Unified TSSE–AITFE Hamiltonian}

Let the AITFE engine state be represented by canonical coordinates $(q,p)$ describing:
\begin{itemize}
  \item Antimatter storage and extraction dynamics.
  \item Pellet compression and ignition variables.
  \item Fusion plasma momentum and energy distribution.
  \item Magnetic nozzle field configuration.
  \item Relativistic exhaust momentum.
\end{itemize}

TSSE requires that the unified Hamiltonian be:
\[
H_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}} =
H_{\text{T}}
+
H_{\text{RPK}}
+
H_{\text{FK}}
+
H_{\text{AITFE}},
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $H_{\text{T}}$ is the TSSE temporal symmetry Hamiltonian.
  \item $H_{\text{RPK}}$ is the relativistic propulsion kernel Hamiltonian.
  \item $H_{\text{FK}}$ is the fusion energetic kernel Hamiltonian.
  \item $H_{\text{AITFE}}$ is the AITFE-specific Hamiltonian governing antimatter extraction,
        pellet injection, hohlraum compression, and magnetic nozzle dynamics.
\end{itemize}

\begin{lemma}[Hamiltonian Layer Compatibility]
If each subsystem Hamiltonian is TSSE-admissible, then their sum is TSSE-admissible.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
TSSE admissibility requires commutation with $\mathcal{T}$, symplectic evolution,
and manifold closure. Each property is preserved under Hamiltonian addition.
\end{proof}

This lemma establishes the unified Hamiltonian foundation of the integrated engine.

