\section{Invariant-Preserving Evolution Operator}

Let $\mathcal{U}(t)$ denote the unified evolution operator generated by
$H_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}$. TSSE requires:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}(t) = J,
\qquad
\det(D\mathcal{U}(t)) = 1,
\qquad
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}} = \mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}.
\]

\begin{theorem}[Unified Symplectic Evolution]
The TSSE–AITFE evolution operator is symplectic and preserves all TSSE invariants.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Each subsystem evolution operator is symplectic. Kernel composition preserves
symplecticity and invariant closure.
\end{proof}

This theorem ensures that the integrated engine evolves within a stable,
invariant-preserving manifold.

